    description: "[REVIEW 2026-11-01, OBSOLETE] Review 2026-11-01 at dev 9ae4abe13f. Deliverable 2 populated dest_access_mode, which ADR-0038 ruling 3 removed (ir.py:141 and slice.py:96 say so). Deliverable 3 cross-references WI-hukoh, which closed done with defer-indefinitely, and the would_admit_dst_reader trigger is gone. Deliverable 1 asks type_hierarchy.py to disambiguate a multi-candidate registry. But _method_return_type_registry (analyze/base.py:4783-4800) is an analyzer-internal, first-writer-wins dict[str,str] that no linker reads, and the ambiguous-candidate problem is now tracked analyzer-side by INV-zujag, WI-jutur and WI-hubik. (Original text below; the review entry in the thread has the evidence.)\n\nPhase 5 (follow-on) of the ADR-0006 Return-Type Registry Pre-Pass. Optional cross-linker integration that consumes the registry built in Phases 1-4.\n\nDELIVERABLES:\n(1) type_hierarchy.py fallback for ambiguous receiver types: when the registry has multiple candidate methods for a given short name, use type_hierarchy's receiver→class index to disambiguate.\n\n(2) dataflow.py refinement for chained method-call access_mode: when a chained call like 'cache.Get(k).Set(v)' has known receiver types (Cache.Get returns *Entry, Entry.Set is a write), populate dest_access_mode for the second call's receiver edge. This is Phase 5's contribution to the WI-hukoh forward-dataflow option (2)/(3) decision.\n\n(3) Cross-reference WI-hukoh in the PR description.\n\nOPTIONAL: only after Phases 1-4 are validated against deep-bakeoff metrics. Skip if the registry signal turns out to be too noisy or too thin to support cross-linker consumption.\n\nPREREQUISITE: Phase 4 (created above)."  # 4ff0
